    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="13">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIAs">II As</ref> 13</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="13" corresp="#wit-h"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="***" target="#IIAs_13.lnote.oe.star3"/><pb n="156" ed="#liebermann"/>Ond we cweðaþ<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#IIAs_13.lnote.oe.20"/>, ðæt ælc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IIAs_13.lnote.oe.9"/> burh sy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IIAs_13.lnote.oe.4"/> gebet XIIII niht ofer gongdagas.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_13.lnote.oe.1"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="13" corresp="#wit-ld"><pb n="156" ed="#liebermann"/>Be burga gebettunge. We cwædon, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ælc burgh sy gebet feowertyne niht ofer gangdagas.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="13" corresp="#wit-ot"><pb n="156" ed="#liebermann"/>[Be burhbot.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IIAs_13.lnote.oe.7"/>] ⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IIAs_13.lnote.oe.5"/> we cwædon, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ælc burh sie g<hi rend="italic">e</hi>bet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#IIAs_13.lnote.oe.20-2"/> feowertyne niht ofer gangdagas.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="13" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="157" ed="#liebermann"/>Quo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#IIAs_13.lnote.oe.28"/> termino burga debent<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#IIAs_13.lnote.oe.29"/> refici. Instituimus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#IIAs_13.lnote.oe.30"/>, ut omne burgum refectum sit XIIII noctibus supra<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#IIAs_13.lnote.oe.31"/> Rogationes.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" n="13" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="134" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be burga gebettunge.]<ptr type="editorNote" n="13" target="#IIAs_13.attnote.fn.13"/> Ond we cweðaþ<ptr type="editorNote" n="14" target="#IIAs_13.attnote.fn.14"/>, ðæt ælc burh sy gebet XIIII niht ofer gongdagas.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="157" ed="#liebermann"/>(Über Herstellung der Burgen. <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi>) Und wir bestimmten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_13.lnote.de.1"/> (-men <hi rend="italic">H</hi>), dass jede Burg<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_13.lnote.de.2"/> 14 Tage nach den Bittgangtagen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_13.lnote.de.3"/> hergerichtet sei.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(On the repair of fortresses. So Ld) And we determined (determine, H) that every fortified town be repaired a fortnight after the Rogation days.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="135" ed="#attenborough"/>And we declare<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_13.attnote.n.1"/> that every fortress shall be repaired by a fortnight after Rogation days<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_13.attnote.n.2"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="421" ed="#whitelock"/>And we pronounce that every borough is to be repaired by a fortnight after Rogation days.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_13.lnote.oe.star3" n="***" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">156</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Raum für Überschrift hier und vor den folgenden Capiteln frei; zu ergänzen aus So Ld Quadr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">space for a heading left blank here and before the following chapters; to be supplied from So Ld Quadr.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_13.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">156</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eðaþ <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eðaþ on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_13.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">156</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">æ <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">æ on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_13.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">156</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_13.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">156</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_13.lnote.oe.28" n="28" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">157</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">De terminis burgorum reficiendorum <hi rend="italic">Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">De terminis burgorum reficiendorum Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_13.lnote.oe.29" n="29" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">157</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">debeant <hi rend="italic">TMHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">debeant TMHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_13.lnote.oe.30" n="30" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">157</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Lond;</hi> Constituimus <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Lond; Constituimus the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_13.lnote.oe.31" n="31" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">157</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">super <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">super T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_13.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">156</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">so So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_13.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">156</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_13.lnote.oe.20-2" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">156</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gebette <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gebette So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_13.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">104</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Hier beginnt ein früherer Sonderabschnitt; <hi rend="italic">s. o.</hi> Einl. 2. <hi rend="italic">Ærest</hi> will Schmid davor setzen, laut des <hi rend="italic">oðer</hi> in 13, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Here an earlier separate section begins; <hi rend="italic">see above</hi> Introduction 2. Schmid would put <hi rend="italic">Ærest</hi> before it, on account of the <hi rend="italic">oðer</hi> in 13, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_13.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">104</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ælfred und seine Kinder und Enkel bauten gegen die Dänen zahlreiche Festungen; über deren Instandhaltung <hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> Burg 5—6 h; <hi rend="italic">trinoda</hi> 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Ælfred and his children and grandchildren built numerous fortresses against the Danes; on their upkeep see <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Burg 5—6 h; <hi rend="italic">trinoda</hi> 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_13.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">104</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. Gl</hi> Bittfahrtstage</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">See <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Bittfahrtstage</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIAs_13.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">208</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">For the significance of this introductory formula (<hi rend="italic">we cweðaþ</hi>), see p. 113, above.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIAs_13.attnote.n.2" n="2" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">208</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Rogation Days are the Monday, Tuesday and Wednesday before Ascension Day.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_13.attnote.fn.13" n="13" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">134</biblScope></bibl><label>gebettunge</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Ld. <hi rend="italic">Be burhbot</hi>. So.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_13.attnote.fn.14" n="14" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">134</biblScope></bibl><label>cweðaþ</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">cwædon</hi>. Ld, Ot.</seg></note>
      </div>
